 # Controlled Luna selection
+
+## Current editorial scope
+
+Both model stages now describe the primary news using `story_type` and
+`is_new_development` (`true`, `false`, or `"unclear"`). This scope correction
+supersedes the older humanitarian calibration below. Luna still keeps credible
+uncertainty Borderline; only its explicit Irrelevant decision excludes metadata.
+The existing detailed enrichment call makes the final evidence-based judgment,
+using configurable Luna or Sol, without another model stage.
+
+Strict selection and fallback both exclude detailed novelty `false` and primary
+`politics_diplomacy`, `conflict_security`, `humanitarian_relief`, or `routine_event`.
+An `explainer_background` or `commentary_opinion` needs novelty explicitly `true`
+to remain eligible. It must actually report a distinct substantive mission
+development; the unchanged scores still apply. Other mission types with novelty
+`"unclear"` continue through the existing thresholds, with conservative significance
+and an explicit evidence gap required by the prompt. A material production,
+fertilizer, commercial-food, water-infrastructure or transition-system consequence
+of conflict uses `supply_disruption` or the corresponding mission type when it is
+the primary development. No title keyword blacklist is involved.
+
+Substantive new sector policy, financing, projects, practical research, systemic
+climate results and transition-material investigations remain valid. Primary
+relief/conflict coverage cannot qualify merely through hunger or agricultural
+references. New model responses must contain both valid scope fields: enrichment
+uses the existing JSON-object API mode plus local field validation; classification
+extends its existing strict JSON schema. Malformed enrichment fails through the
+existing error path with no repair call. Historical in-memory/saved dataclass
+objects default to `other`/`"unclear"`; they are not retroactively reclassified.
+
+JSON/Markdown candidate audits retain both stages' type and novelty, and an explicit
+`editorial_scope_rejection` reason. No Notion property is added. Batch size 100,
+32/48/8 enrichment allowances, 4/5 strict thresholds, 3/3 fallback floors,
+70/20/10 scoring, caps, regional targets and event matching retain their values.
+See the [scope report](../.preview/editorial_scope/20261019/report.md) for exact
+prompt diffs, all regression scenarios, validation and a Luna/Sol dry-run command.
 
